## psc/cli/args.pengu — parser de argv compartido.
##
## Acepta `--flag`, `--flag=value`, `--flag value`, flags cortas y `--`.
## Cada comando declara qué flags consumen valor, cuáles son switches y cuáles
## se acumulan (`-D`).

import psc.sema.names as npool

insignia psc_cli_args_

## Argumentos ya parseados.
##
## ## Memoria
## Strings propios; liberar con `free_parsed`.
rune ParsedArgs:
    values as map of string to string
    switches as map of string to bool
    lists as map of string to list of string
    positionals as list of string

## Resultado del parser.
##
## ## Memoria
## `args` y `error` propios; liberar con `free_parse_result`.
rune ParseResult:
    ok as bool
    error as string
    args as ParsedArgs

## Argumentos vacíos.
##
## ## Memoria
## Mapas/listas propios.
weave empty_args into ParsedArgs:
    return with values is map of string to string, switches is map of string to bool, lists is map of string to list of string, positionals is list of string

## Copia un string.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string owned.
weave copy with s as string into string:
    return calling npool.copy_string with s

## `true` si `xs` contiene `s`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(n).
weave has_str with xs as list of string, s as string into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < xs.len:
        if (xs at i) == s:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false

## Añade una lista vacía para `key` si no existe.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna si ya existe.
weave ensure_list with a as ref to ParsedArgs, key as string into void:
    if not (calling a->lists.has with key):
        calling a->lists.put with (calling copy with key), list of string

## Añade un valor repetible.
##
## ## Memoria
## Copia el valor.
weave add_list with a as ref to ParsedArgs, key as string, value as string into void:
    calling ensure_list with a, key
    var xs as list of string is calling a->lists.get with key
    calling xs.push with (calling copy with value)
    calling a->lists.put with (calling copy with key), xs

## Parser principal.
##
## `value_flags`: flags que consumen el siguiente argv o `=`.
## `switch_flags`: flags booleanas.
## `list_flags`: flags repetibles que consumen valor.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve ParseResult owned.
weave parse with argv as list of string, start as int, value_flags as list of string, switch_flags as list of string, list_flags as list of string into ParseResult:
    var a as ParsedArgs is calling empty_args
    var i as int is start
    var after as bool is false
    while i < argv.len:
        var tok as string is (argv at i)
        if after:
            calling a.positionals.push with (calling copy with tok)
            set i is i + 1
            continue
        if tok == "--":
            set after is true
            set i is i + 1
            continue
        if tok length > 1 and (tok at 0 to 1) == "-":
            var name as string is tok
            var value as string is ""
            var has_value as bool is false
            var eq as int is -1
            var j as int is 1
            while j < tok length:
                if (tok at j to (j + 1)) == "=":
                    set eq is j
                    break
                set j is j + 1
            if eq >= 0:
                set name is tok at 0 to eq
                set value is tok at (eq + 1) to (tok length)
                set has_value is true
            if name == "--help" or name == "-h":
                calling a.switches.put with (calling copy with "help"), true
                set i is i + 1
                continue
            if calling has_str with switch_flags, name:
                calling a.switches.put with (calling copy with name), true
                set i is i + 1
                continue
            var is_value as bool is false
            if calling has_str with value_flags, name:
                set is_value is true
            if calling has_str with list_flags, name:
                set is_value is true
            if is_value:
                if not has_value:
                    if i + 1 >= argv.len:
                        var emsg as string is "missing value for '{name}'"
                        calling free_parsed with (sigil of a)
                        banish name
                        banish value
                        return with ok is false, error is emsg, args is calling empty_args
                    set value is (argv at (i + 1))
                    set i is i + 1
                if calling has_str with list_flags, name:
                    calling add_list with (sigil of a), name, value
                else:
                    if calling a.values.has with name:
                        var old as string is calling a.values.get with name
                        banish old
                    calling a.values.put with (calling copy with name), (calling copy with value)
                banish name
                banish value
                set i is i + 1
                continue
            var uerr as string is "unknown option '{tok}'"
            calling free_parsed with (sigil of a)
            banish name
            banish value
            return with ok is false, error is uerr, args is calling empty_args
        calling a.positionals.push with (calling copy with tok)
        set i is i + 1
    return with ok is true, error is "", args is a

## Valor de un flag, o `""`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string prestado.
weave value with a as ref to ParsedArgs, key as string into string:
    if calling a->values.has with key:
        return calling a->values.get with key
    return ""

## `true` si el switch está activo.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1).
weave enabled with a as ref to ParsedArgs, key as string into bool:
    if calling a->switches.has with key:
        return calling a->switches.get with key
    return false

## Lista de un flag repetible (prestada).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve lista prestada; puede estar vacía.
weave list with a as ref to ParsedArgs, key as string into list of string:
    if calling a->lists.has with key:
        return calling a->lists.get with key
    return list of string

## Primer posicional o `""`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve string prestado.
weave first_positional with a as ref to ParsedArgs into string:
    if a->positionals.len > 0:
        return (a->positionals at 0)
    return ""

## Libera argumentos.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera valores, listas y posicionales.
weave free_parsed with a as ref to ParsedArgs into void:
    for k in a->values:
        var v as string is (a->values at k)
        banish v
    banish a->values
    banish a->switches
    var lv as list of list of string is list of list of string
    for k in a->lists:
        calling lv.push with (a->lists at k)
    banish a->lists
    for xs in lv:
        var xi as int is 0
        while xi < xs.len:
            banish xs at xi
            set xi is xi + 1
        banish xs
    banish lv
    var pi as int is 0
    while pi < a->positionals.len:
        banish a->positionals at pi
        set pi is pi + 1
    banish a->positionals

## Libera un resultado.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera args/error.
weave free_parse_result with r as ref to ParseResult into void:
    banish r->error
    calling free_parsed with (sigil of r->args)
